---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import profileImage from "../assets/images/joe_laskowski.webp";
import locationImage from "../assets/images/south-bend.webp";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About Me | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
  description="Joe Laskowski — twenty-five years in IT, currently working in AI, writing here when I've got something worth saying."
>
  <div class="container">
    <article class="about-content">
      <div class="hero-section">
        <Image
          src={profileImage}
          alt="Joe Laskowski"
          class="profile-image"
          width={180}
          height={180}
          loading="eager"
        />
        <div class="hero-text">
          <h1 class="gradient-text">About Joe Laskowski</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            Twenty-five years in IT, currently working in AI, writing here
            when I've got something worth saying.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2 class="accent-blue">The Work</h2>
        <p>
          Twenty-five years in IT — the first sixteen at small shops, where
          you ARE the IT department and a printer driver counts as a
          credible cause of death. The last nine in enterprise: Microsoft
          365, Active Directory, Intune, Entra ID (which Microsoft has
          renamed enough times that I've stopped keeping count out of
          self-respect), and the infrastructure underneath all of it. Long
          enough, either way, to have watched the same "new" framework get
          rebranded twice and sold back to me. Long enough to have strong
          opinions about why the PowerShell window went red at 2 AM.
        </p>

        <p>
          Since April 2026, I've been the AI Quality Analyst at <a
            href="https://aunalytics.com/">Aunalytics</a
          >, a Midwest data platform company. The job, stripped of its
          title, is this: when the AI says something, is it actually right?
          Turns out that's a more interesting question than the marketing
          for any of these systems would have you believe.
        </p>

        <h2 class="accent-green">Building</h2>
        <p>
          Outside the day job there's <a href="https://autoscript.studio"
            >AutoScript Studio LLC</a
          > — my Indiana company, and the legal wrapper around all the
          things I haven't shipped yet. The brand under it is
          <strong>PixelDrops</strong>, an AI-driven digital-products
          operation: a novel I wrote under a pen name (Amazon launch
          coming), a YouTube channel in build-out, and whatever software I
          ship next. Everything leans hard on AI tooling — that's the
          whole point of doing it now. None of it has launched publicly
          yet. The blog is where the first version of any of it tends to
          surface.
        </p>

        <h2 class="accent-purple">Off the Clock</h2>
        <p>
          Linux every day for nineteen years — the terminal is where I
          think clearest. I keep one eye on crypto, mostly $XRP and $XLM,
          and one hand on whatever AI tooling is currently interesting to
          poke at. Some of what falls out of that ends up on the blog. Most
          of it ends up in a drawer.
        </p>

        <p>
          Away from the screen: double IPAs and stouts thick enough to
          chew, hot wings ordered at a heat level my friends consider a
          personal failing, and Star Wars. I will talk about Star Wars
          longer than is reasonable, and if you let me start ranking the
          films I'm probably your problem for the rest of the evening.
        </p>

        <div class="image-section">
          <Image
            src={locationImage}
            alt="South Bend, Indiana"
            class="location-image"
            width={600}
            height={400}
            loading="eager"
          />
          <p class="image-caption">South Bend, Indiana</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="accent-purple">Family</h2>
        <p>
          Three kids and four grandkids — my two oldest are grown and out
          doing their own thing; AJ, my youngest, is still a kid and is
          with me several days a week. The grandkids are sharper than I
          was at their age and significantly louder. My partner Rianna and
          I started dating on New Year's Day 2025, and between her three
          kids and mine the house is rarely quiet — which, most days, is
          the point.
        </p>

        <p>
          South Bend, Indiana. Real place. Notre Dame, the river, winters
          that make a warm terminal feel like a coping mechanism. I grew
          up here, my kids did too, and I'm not going anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2 class="accent-pink">Let's Connect</h2>
        <p>
          If you want to talk Entra ID, XRP, the right way to deploy
          something at 2 AM, or which Star Wars film is genuinely the best
          one — social links are in the header. The <a href="/">blog</a>
          is whatever I've been chewing on lately. Or <a href="/contact/"
            >send me a message</a
          > and we'll go from there.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <style>
    .about-content {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .hero-section {
      display: flex;
      gap: 3rem;
      align-items: center;
      margin: 3rem 0;
      padding: 2rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    }

    .profile-image {
      width: 180px;
      height: 180px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      border: 4px solid var(--accent-blue);
      box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.2);
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    .hero-text {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .hero-text h1 {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .prose {
      margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .prose h2 {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem 0;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .prose p {
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .prose a {
      color: var(--accent-blue);
      font-weight: 600;
      transition:
        color 0.2s ease,
        text-shadow 0.2s ease;
    }

    .prose a:hover {
      color: var(--accent-cyan);
      text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.3);
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .image-section {
      margin: 3rem 0;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .location-image {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 600px;
      height: auto;
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
      margin: 0 auto 1rem auto;
      display: block;
    }

    .image-caption {
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .hero-section {
        flex-direction: column;
        text-align: center;
        gap: 2rem;
      }

      .hero-text h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      .lead {
        font-size: 1.125rem;
      }

      .profile-image {
        width: 150px;
        height: 150px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
